            <ArticleTitle>Autochthonous Transmission of East/Central/South African Genotype Chikungunya Virus, Brazil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1737-1739</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.161855</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We isolated East/Central/South African genotype chikungunya virus during the 2016 epidemic in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Genome sequencing revealed unique mutations in the nonstructural protein 4 (NSP4-A481D) and envelope protein 1 (E1-K211T). Moreover, all Brazil East/Central/South isolates shared the exclusive mutations E1-M407L and E2-A103T.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
